    "created_at": "2016-09-08T14:01:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-08T14:01:55Z",
    "body": "My hope was that https://github.com/tc39/ecma262/issues/683 would get attention from the appropriate people involved in the JS meta-object-protocol design who would say something like \"oh, clearly the solution is X\". However, that doesn't seem to have happened. So instead I will work harder to understand the exact issue, and either take @saambarati's proposal and turn it into a concrete ECMAScript spec change to move through TC39, or modify HTML in a way to avoid this. Stay tuned...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
